  "note": "Seraph Dive (MOVES.md, Seraph; tapped 54 frames, the fight holds frame 25 while B is held and moves the root through the glide and the dive). The crouch (0-5): the knees bend deep, the fists drop to the hips, the wings lift off the back (x 0 to -30); crouching push box (7.5 m). The hop (6-13): Seraph springs up and forward (root motion 2.0 m forward and 4.0 m up over 6-14), the legs driving straight and then trailing, the wings snapping open to the spread pose by 11. The glide (14-25): the body laid forward 60 degrees, the legs trailing back level with the root (no hurt box below it), the fists by the head, the wings spread with a slow flutter (x +-3); frame 25, the charge frame, is the glide pose with the wings spread full. Push box x +-1.4, y 0-7 from 6 to the touchdown. The dive (26-27): the wings sweep back half folded, the body pitches down and the right fist cocks by the head. Active 28-31: the diving straight, the right arm driving down and forward, the fist leading (the hit box follows the fist and the forearm: x 2.0-5.5, y 1.0-4.5 from the root). Touchdown on 32 (step), on the right knee and the left foot; 33-53 it rises from the knee into the guard, the wings folding by 47. No root motion after the hop: the poses from 26 on are made for the root the fight brings down to the floor by 32 (the legs fold up behind in the dive, nothing more than 1 m below the root on 28, and on 32 the knee and the foot are at the root's height), so the step mark on 32 has no foot on the floor here (a warning). With the wings spread, the fists by the head are inside the box the parts check fits round each wing's plates (not the plates themselves: \"allow\"); the left forearm rests on the knee as it kneels.",
